  "implemented": [
    "PDSTART2 adds two network-order uint32 fields to the original GUI identity: channel1..4 and an explicit nonzero pan ID. Header selects exactly48 legacy or56 selected bytes under one2s deadline. Validation precedes the installation transaction lease.",
    "PDSTART1 retains legacy channel1/observed-pan discovery. Partial or malformed explicit selection is rejected; no configured-to-legacy retry or fallback is implemented.",
    "Typed selection is carried through service launch, radio constructor and ordinary-user IQ source. The created stream and selected pan must agree with requested channel, pan and original GUI owner.",
    "Canonical private readiness includes the channel. The constructor checks the requested pair before capture startup and passes the same channel and observed pan to the DSP via its fixed environment.",
    "The existing DSP binding guard is exercised on all four channels: incomplete owner readback blocks admission; binding loss invalidates correction and armed/running source; later matching readback cannot resurrect the failed session.",
    "Root peer/executable checks, installation lease, fixed ARP destination, capture filter, descriptor ownership, privilege drop and scheduling limits remain unchanged. No new command/path/network/scheduler input."
  ],
